"""kaltstart - unlock a remote LUKS root with a FIDO2 token that stays local.

The token is never exposed to the server. This workstation tool asks the
token for an hmac-secret value (fido2-assert from fido2-tools) and pipes the
result, as an ordinary LUKS passphrase, into Debian's stock cryptroot-unlock
over SSH (dropbear-initramfs). There is no custom code on the server.

Secret handling: the passphrase lives only in process memory and on stdin
pipes of child processes. It never appears in argv, the environment, local
files, log output or exception messages.
"""

